<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000016> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> "A disposition is an entity that causes a specific process or transformation in an entity in which it inheres, under specific circumstances and in conjunction with the laws of nature. For example, the disposition of vegetables to decay when not refrigerated, the disposition of blood to coagulate, the disposition of a patient with a weakened immune system to contract disease." .
<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000016> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000016> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "disposition" .
<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000016> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000020> .
<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000020> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> "An experimental factor which is a property or characteristic of some other entity.  For example, the mouse has the colour white." .
<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000020> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000020> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "material property" .
<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000020> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/efo/EFO_0000001> .
<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000020> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "SpecificallyDependentContinuant" .
<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000020> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "specifically dependent continuant" .
<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0000001> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> "A disease is a disposition to undergo pathological processes that exists in an organism because of one or more disorders in that organism." .
<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0000001> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> "review target in EFO from disease_terms_review_enriched.csv" .
